.TITLE "man"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the reference manuals for commands, functions, and configuration files. It is the primary source of __on-system documentation__ for Linux.

.DIV "TLDR"
**man command**
Displays the manual page for a specific command.
> __command__ the tool to look up

**man -k keyword**
Searches for manual pages that contain a specific keyword in their description.
> __-k__ keyword search flag | __keyword__ the search term

**man section command**
Opens a manual page from a specific section (e.g., section 1 for user commands).
> __section__ manual section number | __command__ the tool to look up

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Navigating a manual page is similar to using __less__; use the arrow keys to scroll and press __q__ to exit. If you are unsure of a command's name, __man -k__ is a great way to discover related utilities.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"


documentation: __https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/man.1.html__
